ps://api.github.com/users/xxxxxwater/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"D1 does not record which retry predicate failed or its scan elapsed/attempts. This adds opt-in D2 memory capture at the original predicate and a default-off, versioned companion export after strict owned cleanup. Capsules have fixed phase/catalogue fields, a 4096-byte cap, O_EXCL/fsync publication, shared cleanup32 accounting, an explicit manifest allowlist and a verifier bound to the same controller SHA.\n\nThe base is PR35 `delivery/m05-control-package-fix@9b61e5f35dd2196ef2fdddfa03559eca3f1322ec`. Its two literal package fixes and all prior evidence remain. The controller is byte-identical to reviewed source `8594a35827b0e064584113de48fda2490cb1c98e` (SHA256 `67a97e551590ff4f23d1256c79ad5b9ae0259e9973012541cee678ab1842ca93`). UTA runtime is unchanged from 6010.\n\nValidation evidence is limited to two preserved first runs on different sources: source3040 ran120 entries (99 declared+21 inherited) for memory D2/disabled interface and related regressions; source8594 ran76 entries (29export+24D2/interface+23D1), CPU2/child0/exit0, with independent PURE_ONLY raw review. These are overlapping scopes, not a combined196-test result. This assembled delivery tree has not run new tests, packaging or CI; its four-file76 closure matches source8594. Static MANIFEST selection covers the new paths, no new .sha256 was added, and actual new-source sdist/wheel/archive closure remains NOT_RUN. The wheel still only contains the configured uta package.\n\n`D2_COMPANION_EXPORT_ENABLED=False`. Kernel-space support remains NOT_IMPLEMENTED/NOT_VERIFIED; no quota/mount capability is assumed. Enabling D2 requires a separately reviewed controller source SHA and execution scope. The generic public JSON verifier deliberately tightens to finite strict JSON/no duplicate keys/4MiB even while export is off. Existing D1 synchronous I/O remains. The cleanup proxy relies on fixed909's verified inherited-session call chain and normal-return empty-group assertion; it is not a hostile/noescape sandbox, and leader/EOF booleans alone do not establish closure. Optional export faults retain the original primary; fsync has no proven completion bound or directory crash durability.\n\nD1's nine fields, scan3/50ms predicates, case/escrow budgets, cleanup32/total192, host gates, 900s fresh gate, business argv and four closed-stream contents/protocol remain. M05 stays UNKNOWN/P_NOT_RUN and05spent; new fields cannot be backfilled into that run. No actual GHA/M06 registration, activation, perf-ref write, 10k/s, HA or real-funds approval is included.\n\nDelivery remains OFF for review. A future synthetic activation requires a new source/ref/profile, fresh900s workspace approval and exact root scope while retaining20/s×10s/2shard and original B/P budgets. A reviewed rollback restores the controller to PR35 and removes the matching two new test modules while retaining all first evidence and package fixes. See `docs/m0-d2-default-off-delivery.md` for the boundaries and the safe evidence records.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T03:34:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T03:34:23Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"81b1d4f08c96ca3b3ad83108af07f4199eba1c86","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"PureGamma-Harness:delivery/m0-d2-companion-default-off","ref":"delivery/m0-d2-companion-default-off","repo":{"id":1457814529,"node_id":"R_kgDOVuR8AQ","name":"uta-unified-account","full_name":"PureGamma-Harness/uta-unified-account","owner":{"login":"PureGamma-Harness","id":352528293,"node_id":"O_kgDOFQMnpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/352528293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PureGamma-Harness","html_url":"https://github.com/PureGamma-Harness","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PureGamma-Harnes